1
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,957
Welcome to the ward.

2
00:00:08,707 --> 00:00:12,078
Feeling a bit nervous before surgery is completely normal.

3
00:00:12,828 --> 00:00:14,832
To help you feel prepared and relaxed,

4
00:00:14,832 --> 00:00:18,524
let's walk through what your day will look like, from start to finish.

5
00:00:22,124 --> 00:00:24,385
Your day begins right here in the ward.

6
00:00:25,135 --> 00:00:27,354
Our nursing team will help you get ready.

7
00:00:28,104 --> 00:00:30,664
You will change into a clean hospital gown.

8
00:00:31,414 --> 00:00:34,765
We will ask you to remove any jewellery, hairpins, dentures,

9
00:00:34,765 --> 00:00:38,283
or glasses for your safety, and check your identification band.

10
00:00:41,883 --> 00:00:42,710
When it is time,

11
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:46,897
you will be comfortably wheeled down to the operating theatre suite by our staff.

12
00:00:47,647 --> 00:00:49,503
Don't worry, you won't be alone.

13
00:00:50,253 --> 00:00:54,790
Our theatre nurses and your anaesthetist will greet you as soon as you arrive,

14
00:00:54,790 --> 00:00:58,338
double-checking your details to ensure everything is correct.

15
00:01:01,938 --> 00:01:04,498
Next, you will enter the anaesthesia area.

16
00:01:05,248 --> 00:01:08,356
We will attach gentle monitoring stickers to your chest,

17
00:01:08,356 --> 00:01:10,242
a blood pressure cuff on your arm,

18
00:01:10,242 --> 00:01:14,293
and a small clip on your finger to monitor your breathing and heart rate.

19
00:01:15,043 --> 00:01:17,081
Your anaesthetist will talk to you,

20
00:01:17,081 --> 00:01:20,924
place a small IV line in your hand or arm, and before you know it,

21
00:01:20,924 --> 00:01:23,427
you will drift off into a safe, deep sleep.

22
00:01:27,027 --> 00:01:28,753
When your surgery is finished,

23
00:01:28,753 --> 00:01:31,687
you will wake up in the Post-Anaesthesia Care Unit,

24
00:01:31,687 --> 00:01:33,470
often called the recovery room.

25
00:01:34,220 --> 00:01:36,695
You might feel a little sleepy or groggy.

26
00:01:37,445 --> 00:01:40,950
Our dedicated recovery nurses will be right by your side,

27
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:43,779
monitoring your vital signs, keeping you warm,

28
00:01:43,779 --> 00:01:46,362
and making sure your pain is well-managed.

29
00:01:49,962 --> 00:01:51,863
Once you are fully awake and stable,

30
00:01:51,863 --> 00:01:55,295
you will be transferred back to your bed in the orthopaedic ward.

31
00:01:56,045 --> 00:01:58,746
Here, you can rest, sip some water when permitted,

32
00:01:58,746 --> 00:02:02,040
and begin your recovery journey with our team supporting you.

33
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:05,435
Remember, we are always just a call bell away.

34
00:02:09,035 --> 00:02:12,247
If you have any questions at all about your procedure today,

35
00:02:12,247 --> 00:02:14,923
please don't hesitate to ask your doctor or nurse.

36
00:02:15,673 --> 00:02:17,081
We are here for you.

37
00:02:17,831 --> 00:02:20,093
Wishing you a very smooth recovery.

